written("w11_n_greater_than_one", 11, 4, "11e",
        stem="Explain why the refractive index of any transparent material is greater than 1, and what this means for the angles of incidence and refraction when light enters the material from air.",
        points=[P("refractive index = c ÷ v, and light is always slower in a material than in a vacuum, so the ratio is greater than 1", ["c ÷ v", "c / v", "speed in a vacuum divided by", "always slower", "slower in the material", "cannot travel faster than", "nothing travels faster", "fastest in a vacuum"]),
                P("since n = sin i ÷ sin r > 1, sin r is less than sin i", ["sin i ÷ sin r", "sin i / sin r", "sin r is smaller", "sin r is less", "sin i is greater"]),
                P("so the angle of refraction is less than the angle of incidence: the ray bends towards the normal", ["angle of refraction is less", "angle of refraction is smaller", "r is less than i", "r < i", "towards the normal", "smaller than the angle of incidence"])],
        min_points=2,
        model_answer="Refractive index is the speed of light in a vacuum divided by its speed in the material. Light travels fastest in a vacuum and is slower in every material, so the ratio is always greater than 1. Since n also equals sin i ÷ sin r, sin r must be smaller than sin i, so the angle of refraction is smaller than the angle of incidence and the ray bends towards the normal on entering the material.",
        hints=["Write the definition of n in terms of speeds. Which speed is always the larger?",
               "Now use n = sin i ÷ sin r. If n > 1, how do the two sines compare?",
               "Explain why n > 1 and what it implies for the angles."],
        keywords="n = c/v > 1 because light is slower in materials; so sin r < sin i, r < i",
        sample_pass=["n = c/v and light is slower in any material than in a vacuum, so n > 1; therefore sin r < sin i and the angle of refraction is smaller",
                     "light cannot travel faster than in a vacuum so the ratio is above 1, meaning the ray bends towards the normal with r less than i"],
        sample_fail=["Because glass is thicker than air", "n is greater than 1 because the angle of refraction is bigger"])

