        min_points=2,
        model_answer="As the object moves from beyond 2F towards F, the real inverted image moves further from the lens, from between F and 2F to beyond 2F, and grows: it is diminished at first, the same size as the object when the object is at 2F, and magnified when the object is between 2F and F. When the object reaches F the refracted rays emerge parallel and no image is formed.",
